A||||4||fierose||Steering Rack from Autozone||||6||
Z||000000||fierose||03-11-2001||10:48 PM||||I'm pretty sure I had read someone in the forum had purchased a steering rack from autozone and had said that it came with inner tie rods.  I coudn't see why they would do that but I didn't want to order some new ones if they were coming with the rack.  Can anyone help me out on what actually comes with the rack from autozone, and maybe some tips on doing the job including trying to get away without an alignment afterwards.<P>TIA||||reg||6
Z||000001||bHooper||03-11-2001||10:55 PM||||the autozone rack includes inner tie rods, and thats it.<P>you will need to swap frame bushings, and nuts from your old one.<P>it does not come with outer tie rod ends... which you may want to replace anyway.<P>i have used one, and so has Bob Englert.<P>good luck!<P>hoop||||reg||12
Z||000002||Bob Englert||03-11-2001||11:00 PM||||I have had good results with the racks from AutoZone.  Much better than the racks I got from Advance Auto (which I returned).<P>Remember that there are 2 types available. the 3 turn (performance version?) which was used on the GT's and the 84's, and the 3 1/2 turn version (standard) which was used on the 85-88 non GT's.<P>They are interchagable.  The 3 1/2 turn rack will provide a little lower steering effort, the 3 turn rack should be a little more responsive.  Your choice.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierose||03-12-2001||01:00 PM||||Thanks for the help guys.  I'm on spring break from purdue and need to get this done this week or I won't have a car to drive back this weekend.  Just hoping I can get the tie rod ends off without damaging them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||03-12-2001||01:29 PM||||They come with new inner tie-rods but not outer.||||reg||1
